            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Rescue&quot; abciximab for complicated percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>800-3, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the in-hospital outcome of 138 consecutive patients who received abciximab as a &quot;rescue&quot; intervention for complicated coronary angioplasty in a high-risk clinical setting. &quot;Rescue&quot; treatment with abciximab was associated with clinical and angiographic success rates of 83% and 84%, respectively, whereas the risk of bleeding was higher in patients of low body weight.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
